{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27116249","formula":"C₂₆H₂₉NO₂","hill":"C26H29NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":26.0,"H":29.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Droloxifene"},"descriptions":{"en":"Droloxifene (INN, USAN) (former developmental code names FK-435, ICI-79280, K-060, K-21060E, RP-60850), also known as 3-hydroxytamoxifen, is a nonsteroidal selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) of the triphenylethylene group that was developed originally in Germany and later in Japan for the treatment of breast cancer, osteoporosis in men and postmenopausal women, and cardiovascular disorders but was abandoned and never marketed. It reached phase II and phase III clinical trials for these indications before development was discontinued in 2000. The drug was found to be significantly less effective than tamoxifen in the treatment of breast cancer in two phase III clinical trials."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":3033767,"mass":387.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC/C(=C(/C1=CC=C(C=C1)OCCN(C)C)\\C2=CC(=CC=C2)O)/C3=CC=CC=C3","inchikey":"ZQZFYGIXNQKOAV-OCEACIFDSA-N","iupac":"3-[(E)-1-[4-[2-(dimethylamino)ethoxy]phenyl]-2-phenylbut-1-enyl]phenol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3033767","atoms":58,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.695,"y":0.487,"z":1.111,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.672,"y":3.46,"z":1.71,"el":"O"},{"x":6.997,"y":0.794,"z":-0.497,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.741,"y":0.09,"z":-0.196,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.355,"y":-1.127,"z":-0.392,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.331,"y":0.193,"z":0.144,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.83,"y":-1.359,"z":-0.686,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.583,"y":1.321,"z":-0.341,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.579,"y":-2.387,"z":-0.267,"el":"C"},{"x":0.624,"y":0.294,"z":-0.868,"el":"C"},{"x":0.067,"y":0.191,"z":1.481,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.661,"y":-1.538,"z":0.579,"el":"C"},{"x":2.365,"y":0.39,"z":0.791,"el":"C